# x86_64 baseline of the final hardening build.
# Measured locally with scripts/check-sizes.sh on the reference desktop,
# built from commit 70e9984 (tree clean apart from documentation), rustc
# 1.98.1 from rust-toolchain.toml, release profile (fat LTO,
# codegen-units=1, panic=abort, strip). The sources of the shipped
# binaries changed since the previous baseline (420a714) by the second
# buffer's first-touch move, the Undo/Trash ownership rule and the
# measurement markers.
# The per-area account of the growth over the Plan 7 baseline
# (inacircle 900352 671864) is in docs/benchmarks/binary-size.md.
# Refreshed after the pages-to-PDF work on this x86_64 desktop, built from
# commit 8cf5df2 (tree clean), same toolchain and profile: inacircle grew
# 1112 B (file) and the pages family 3224 B; the shipped inacircle does not
# link the new zip, flate, probe or pdf crates.
# Refreshed after the many-inputs-to-one-output work on this x86_64 desktop,
# built from commit 9f808bcd (tree clean), same toolchain and profile: inacircle
# grew 40472 B (file) and the pages family 13352 B (file, 12432 B of .text), both under the
# 100 KB explanation threshold; the shipped inacircle still does not link
# the zip, flate, probe or pdf crates.
# Refreshed after the wheel drop-list and memory work (list limit, paths held
# once, owned uri-list parser), same toolchain and profile: inacircle grew
# 3592 B (file, 3024 B of .text); the other two binaries are unchanged.
# Refreshed after the CBZ work (images to CBZ, the stored-ZIP writer, the
# image header probe, the catalog's failure backoff), same toolchain and
# profile, built from commit 62f592bd (tree clean; later commits touch only
# fuzz corpora and tests, and the shrinking-source check in the ZIP writer,
# which added 32 B to inacircle-pages): inacircle grew 9312 B (file, 8544 B
# of .text), from the backoff bookkeeping and the typed stop reason;
# inacircle-pages grew 39088 B (file, 31056 B of .text), from the ZIP writer,
# the PNG/JPEG header sniffer and
# the CBZ join action. Both are under the 100 KB explanation threshold;
# inacircle-text is unchanged; the shipped inacircle still does not link the
# zip, flate, probe or pdf crates.
# Refreshed after the GFM work (tables, strikethrough, task lists and extended
# autolinks in the Markdown reader; the aligned and listed table layout in the
# plain-text writer), same toolchain and profile, built from commit f811cc5c
# (tree clean): inacircle-text grew 61456 B (file, 53136 B of .text), from the
# table parser and the column-width and wrapping logic. That is under the
# 100 KB explanation threshold and the .text stays under the 1 MiB family
# limit; inacircle and inacircle-pages are unchanged. +416 B of .text (+416 B
# file) from the closing fixes (wrap at runs of spaces, control characters warn).
# Refreshed after the EPUB and HTML work (Markdown and plain text to an
# EPUB book or one HTML page), same toolchain and profile, built from commit
# 31ced7b5 (tree clean; the commits after the last source change touch only
# fuzz corpora): inacircle-text grew 103096 B (file, 87606 B of .text). That
# is just over the 100 KB explanation threshold; the .text (538472 B) stays
# far under the 1 MiB family limit. The growth is new code in this binary:
# the XHTML writer (heading anchors, link and image policy, character
# filter; about 39 KB of symbols), the EPUB packer (package document,
# navigation, chapter split, UUID and timestamp; about 20 KB), the ZIP
# writer (about 3 KB; the stored-entry writer already existed for the CBZ
# work), the book and HTML action code (about 30 KB, with the language and
# title rules), and the rest is formatting, hashing and allocation code
# monomorphised for them. Symbol sizes are from an unstripped build of the
# same sources (nm), an approximation under LTO inlining. inacircle grew
# 6368 B (file, 4880 B of .text), from the new action rows, presets and the
# language environment passed to the child; inacircle-pages grew 496 B. The
# shipped inacircle still does not link the doc, zip or epub crates.
# After the closing fixes: inacircle-text grew 1552 B (file, 1200 B of .text)
# from the URL validity checks in the XHTML writer (percent escapes, one
# fragment, authority brackets) and the create-new write of the HTML page.
# Refreshed after the Markdown-and-images join to one EPUB book, same toolchain
# and profile, built from commit 715b5b2b (tree clean; the commits after the
# last source change touch only fuzz corpora). inacircle grew 15584 B (file,
# 14736 B of .text) from the new action row, the preset's mixed-selection
# rule and the count of documents plus usable images; inacircle-text grew
# 67904 B (file, 59776 B of .text), both under the 100 KB explanation
# threshold: the image reference resolution (lexical path normalisation,
# percent decoding, file identity), the JPEG and PNG check, the image
# chapter and package entries, and the join over documents. The .text
# (599448 B) stays far under the 1 MiB family limit. inacircle-pages is
# unchanged. The shipped inacircle still does not link the doc, zip or epub
# crates.
# Refreshed after the EPUB reader (EPUB to plain text), same toolchain and
# profile, built from commit 999793bc (tree clean). inacircle-text grew
# 190256 B (file, 168491 B of .text), over the 100 KB explanation threshold.
# The growth is code new to this binary: the first link of the xml crate
# (parser, namespace handling, the HTML5 entity table, UTF-16 decoding), the
# EPUB package reader (container, package document, spine, encryption
# check, ZIP entry limits) and the XHTML reader that builds the document
# tree, plus the text action around them and the formatting code
# monomorphised for them. The .text (767939 B) stays under the 1 MiB family
# limit. inacircle grew 632 B (file, 368 B of .text) from the new action row
# and preset; inacircle-pages is unchanged. The shipped inacircle still does
# not link the xml, doc, zip or epub crates.
# Refreshed after the EPUB to Markdown work (the EPUB book as a Markdown file
# with its images), same toolchain and profile, built from commit 34950b25
# (tree clean; the commits after the last source change touch only fuzz
# corpora). inacircle-text grew 123528 B (file, 111760 B of .text), over the
# 100 KB explanation threshold. The growth is the GFM writer's mark logic
# (escapes, the autolink guards that keep the output stable when read back,
# table and strikethrough output) and the epub-to-markdown action around it
# (the metadata pass, the unique heading slugs for internal links, the image
# copy and naming, the output folder), plus the formatting code
# monomorphised for them. The .text (879699 B) stays under the 1 MiB family
# limit. inacircle grew 264 B (file, 16 B of .text) from the new action row
# and preset; inacircle-pages is unchanged. The shipped inacircle still does
# not link the xml, doc, zip or epub crates.
# Refreshed after the code page work (8-bit text classification and the
# Windows-1250 and ISO-8859-2 to UTF-8 actions), same toolchain and profile,
# built from commit 69ab9ad8 (tree clean; the commits after the last source
# change touch only fuzz corpora). inacircle-text grew 24712 B (file, 21392 B
# of .text): the code page decoder with its two 128-entry tables, the UTF-8
# census that rejects text that is already UTF-8, and the action around them;
# under the 100 KB explanation threshold, and the .text (901091 B) stays
# under the 1 MiB family limit. inacircle grew 13072 B (file, 10912 B of
# .text): the classifier's 8-bit text detection with its bounded re-read, and
# the new group and two presets. inacircle-pages is unchanged. The shipped
# inacircle still does not link the xml, doc, zip or epub crates.
# Refreshed after the subtitle actions (the SRT, WebVTT and ASS readers and
# writers, the four conversion actions, the classifier's subtitle types), same
# toolchain and profile, built from commit 780ad0fe6 (tree clean). Growth since
# the previous line: inacircle +3360 B file (+1808 B .text), the engine's
# subtitle classifier and anything else changed since that line; inacircle-text
# +104 B file (-48 B .text); inacircle-pages +10440 B file (+8416 B .text), a
# binary whose direct dependencies do not include the engine or the subtitle
# crate, so not from this work and not attributed here; inacircle-subtitles
# +13400 B file (+11248 B .text) since its own line, which is the subtitle code.
# Every growth is under the 100 KB explanation threshold and every .text is
# under the 1 MiB family limit. The aarch64 baseline is not refreshed.
# Added with the subtitle family's first binary, inacircle-subtitles, built from
# commit b2e797e0 plus the new crate's sources, same toolchain and profile: a
# new binary, so no growth is measured; its .text (343843 B) is far under the
# 1 MiB family limit. The other lines are not refreshed here.
# Refreshed at the close of the subtitle work, same toolchain and profile, built
# from commit 666f61b18 (tree clean). Growth since the previous line: inacircle
# +64 B file (-160 B .text), from the engine's subtitle head search and the
# engine's check of subtitle outputs as text, both since the previous line;
# inacircle-text and inacircle-pages are unchanged; inacircle-subtitles +6840 B
# file (+6272 B .text), the subtitle code since its previous line (the reader
# fixes from the fuzzing and review rounds: the speaker-name, markup, override
# and white-space rules, and the WebVTT and ASS fixes). Every growth is under
# the 100 KB explanation threshold and every .text is under the 1 MiB family
# limit. The aarch64 baseline is not refreshed.
# Refreshed after the TTML reader and the two TTML actions (the xml-based
# reader in crates/subtitles, the actions, the classifier's TTML type), same
# toolchain and profile, built from the tree this commit records. inacircle-subtitles
# grew 343352 B (file) and 136354 B (.text), past the 100 KB explanation
# threshold. By symbol name on an unstripped build of the same tree, 72.5 KB is
# the TTML reader (the subtitles::ttml module); the xml crate, linked into this
# binary for the first time, shows about 4.8 KB by name, so most of its code is
# inlined into the TTML symbols and is not split further. The HTML5 entity table
# of the xml crate is linked as well (about 77 KB of relocated data in
# .data.rel.ro), though TTML reads with html_entities off: a candidate for a
# later change to the xml crate, not made here. The .text (497717 B) stays far
# under the 1 MiB family limit. inacircle grew 1760 B (file, 1552 B of .text)
# since its previous line, under the threshold; inacircle-text and
# inacircle-pages are unchanged.
# Refreshed at the close of the TTML work, same toolchain and profile, built
# from commit 379f4bdb5 (tree clean). Growth since the previous line:
# inacircle-subtitles +10424 B file (+9664 B .text): the TTML reader's fixes
# since that line (hidden text, refused animated visibility, the initial
# values, the reasons for no subtitles); under the 100 KB explanation
# threshold, and its .text stays under the 1 MiB family limit. inacircle
# -272 B file (-848 B .text) net, from the classifier's TTML root scan and
# the menu's TTML rows since that line. The other two binaries are unchanged.
# The aarch64 baseline is not refreshed.
inacircle 1200856 925144
inacircle-text 1268024 901043
inacircle-pages 514648 412179
inacircle-subtitles 804792 507381
